    "body": "## Change\n\nThe current model retains required answer words but still fails some wording/role transfers. The programme had overlapping integration, qualification and research trackers, while several documentation entry points still described repaired failures or superseded schedules as current.\n\nAdopt the owner-approved immediate sequence: #1137 learned role-aware source selection shared with response commitment → #1138 exact learned relational memory → #1139 selective geometric access at complete measured cost → #1140 typed operator composition for conversation and Rust reasoning. Each issue has a concrete behavioral handoff and failure branch; closing a negative experiment does not satisfy a capability prerequisite. Broader capability and release work follows those accepted handoffs.\n\nReconcile the canonical plan, current-state, root roadmap, research/lifecycle entry points, component READMEs and archived instructions. Add the research synthesis, including source-derived limits on the archived angular-routing comparison. Correct the README to the #1136 results while preserving artifact, provenance and capability boundaries. Historical measurements and original experimental contracts remain preserved.\n\nGitHub is already reconciled: four new child issues with native dependencies, #1137 assigned, programme tracker #820 and milestone 21 updated. Superseded #1083, #1084, #1087, #1089, #1090, #1091 and #940 are closed as not planned with preserved original bodies and explicit successor ownership. Remaining broader issues have current scopes and blockers. This PR does not close the four build issues or claim their mechanisms are implemented.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py`: passed.\n- Existing native `r4-policy-check .`: passed; no model behavior evaluated.\n- All 74 newly added local Markdown links resolve.\n- Live GitHub graph: 13 open issues, expected parents/blockers and no dependency cycles; submitted issue bodies and closure states verified.\n- Documentation only: no Rust changes, model training, model evaluation or release campaign. Protected CI retains its existing required checks; compatibility acknowledgements are not broad QA results.\n\nThe cumulative model ledger remains 1,081.641/1,800 seconds. The plan carries the one-task/one-agent budget-friendly cadence and preauthorized necessary storage increases. Intentional changes and untracked material in the owner's main checkout are untouched.\n",
